<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on very good demand and heavy offerings.  Select and Choice chuck and round cuts lower, while the rib and loin cuts generally steady. Beef trimmings weak on fairly good demand and moderate to heavy offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>  464 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>   93 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>15 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     102.08	102.29	 96.85	 96.29</p>
<p>		   -1.12	 -1.32	 -0.81	 -0.33</p>
<p>Rib	  165.98	165.94	157.70	157.94</p>
<p>Chuck	 64.94	 64.33	 65.35	 62.88</p>
<p>Round	 82.69	 82.69	 81.05	 81.05</p>
<p>Loin	 170.29	172.16	151.49	152.20</p>
<p>Brisket     60.84	 60.84	 59.48	 59.48</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  66.76	 66.67	 67.01	 66.83</p>
<p>Flank	 58.71	 58.71	 57.72	 57.72</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
